  "title": "What are auroras? 🌌",
  "hook": "What are those lights dancing in the sky near the poles?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_hook",
      "narration": "What are those lights dancing in the sky near the poles?",
      "on_screen_text": "What are auroras?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "auroras?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_wind",
      "narration": "It all starts with the Sun, which blasts out a stream of electrically charged particles: the solar wind.",
      "on_screen_text": "The solar wind",
      "highlight_words": [
        "wind"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_shield",
      "narration": "Earth has an invisible shield, its magnetic field, that deflects almost all of those particles.",
      "on_screen_text": "Earth's magnetic shield",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shield"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_poles",
      "narration": "But near the poles, the field lines guide them down into the atmosphere, forming a ring of light.",
      "on_screen_text": "A ring over the poles",
      "highlight_words": [
        "ring"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_collide",
      "narration": "There they crash into oxygen and nitrogen in the air, and every collision makes those gases glow.",
      "on_screen_text": "Collisions that glow",
      "highlight_words": [
        "glow"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_colors",
      "narration": "Oxygen gives the green and, higher up, the red; nitrogen paints the purple tones.",
      "on_screen_text": "Each gas, a color",
      "highlight_words": [
        "color"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_south",
      "narration": "And it happens at both poles: northern lights in the north and southern lights in the south.",
      "on_screen_text": "North and south",
      "highlight_words": [
        "south"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_storm",
      "narration": "When the Sun has a strong storm, the ring grows and auroras show up much closer to the equator.",
      "on_screen_text": "Solar storms",
      "highlight_words": [
        "storms"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_jupiter",
      "narration": "And they're not just on Earth: Jupiter has auroras so big the whole Earth would fit inside.",
      "on_screen_text": "Auroras on Jupiter!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Jupiter!"
