  "description": "The solar wind sends charged particles toward Earth; the magnetic field deflects most of them, but near the poles it guides them into the atmosphere. There they hit oxygen (green and red) and nitrogen (purple) and make the sky glow. It happens at both poles, strong solar storms push auroras closer to the equator, and Jupiter has auroras bigger than Earth. Original 3D animation; not to scale.",
